MID_SE_Lou_Buc_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_C_001: Hm? You can come in.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_C_002: Sorry for interrupting, but there's something I wanted\nto...to talk to you about...
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_C_003: Hm...
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_C_004: Um... Why are you looking at me like that?
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_C_005: Ah, sorry. I was just thinking that your cheerful\ndisposition reminds me of your sister.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_C_006: You remember my sister? Surely you haven't seen\nher for 10 years, at least.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_C_007: I remember everyone I've trained. And she made\nquite an impression on me.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_C_008: She didn't hesitate to tell me she was the daughter of\nGeneral Senghor and had come to me on his orders.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_C_009: She'd heard rumors about me before arriving in\nCydonia and decided it was best to be direct.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_C_010: Yes, I read as much in her letters. She said, "There is\nno need to deceive the Demon Bear of Baphos."
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_C_011: My sister is usually much more cautious than I am,\nbut she has her bold moments as well.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_C_012: She has always been exceptional though. I've never\nseen her make a mistake. I admire that!
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_C_013: Yes, she was an excellent student. And when bandits\nattacked, I saw firsthand how superb her skills were.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_C_014: Well, of course! Though...I did hear of one mistake\nshe made.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_C_015: She fell in love with someone in Cydonia, it seems.\nBut her feelings weren't reciprocated in the end.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_C_016: She...fell in love? There must be some mistake. She\nwas very serious and focused only on training.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_C_017: There's no mistake! I have proof!
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_C_018: I'll show you next time. Then we can figure out who\nthis mystery person is together!
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_C_019: Ludia...is that why you wanted to talk to me?
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_C_020: Yep! Sure is! And I can't wait to see what we can\nfind out!
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_C_021: We? You're the only one who finds this matter of\ninterest. Are you even listening to me?
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B_001: Here it is, Buccar! Proof my sister fell in love!
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B_002: So you found the letter she sent you.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B_003: That's right. This is the letter where she wrote\nsomeone had caught her eye!
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B_004: Hrm.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B_005: She says, "While the mission comes first, I now have\na goal beyond the Demon Bear's techniques."
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B_006: And afterward, she wrote about this person in every\nletter, so...this has to be it! Do you know anything?
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B_007: As I said before, she was the epitome of seriousness\nin my eyes.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B_008: Besides, why dig this up now? I know little about\nromance, but still this business seems long past.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B_009: You have a point... She's married now—into\na noble family, to a completely different man.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B_010: The person she fell in love with may have even died\nin the Cydonia Massacre...
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B_011: But this was the only thing I've ever seen my sister\ntruly passionate about! Ever!
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B_012: I want to know the truth of what happened,\nto understand why it didn't work out!
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B_013: You want to uncover a truth from the past, eh? Only\nsomeone who was there at the time could do that.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B_014: I will help you.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B_015: Thank you so much! I believe this letter holds an\nimportant clue...
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B_016: She mentioned spending all day with this person,\ntraining, and...wanting to spend all night with him.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B_017: It seems she tried asking him out during breaks in\nher training... You didn't notice anything, Buccar?
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B_018: Hmm? We trained all day on several occasions,\nbut we did not speak to anyone else.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B_019: Really? She didn't sneak away with someone\nbetween sessions or anything?!
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B_020: No, never. She stayed close at hand during our\nbreaks as well.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B_021: How is that possible? She definitely said... Hmm...\nWait... Of course!
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B_022: Um, Buccar... When the two of you were training,\ndid she ever ask you what you were doing afterward?
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B_023: Yes, she did. And I always explained my plans for\nthe next training session so she could prepare.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B_024: And...did she ever ask about what you look for\nin a woman?
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B_025: She did. I couldn't think of much to say, so I told her\nhow Lady Leda had impressed me.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B_026: Milady was smart even as a youngster, and she was\na talented singer and dancer too.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B_027: I remember your sister fell silent when I said that.\nSo I quickly explained I hadn't meant it romantically.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B_028: *sigh*
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B_029: Is something wrong?
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B_030: The mystery has been solved... I understand now\nhow my sister's romance fell apart...
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B_031: What's wrong? Isn't that a good thing?\nShe eventually married someone else after all.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B_032: No, it's not a good thing! Do you know nothing\nof love or romance at all?!
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_B_033: Why are you so angry? I...don't understand.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_A_001: The rations for the next march have been delivered.\nOur transaction has concluded.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_A_002: Thank you for the hard work and prompt delivery.\nThe Vandahl Trading Company never disappoints.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_A_003: We appreciate your continued patronage. Now,\nI'll be going.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_A_004: My interactions with Ludia have become so\nbusinesslike of late.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_A_005: I had been enjoying her polite-but-spirited attitude.\nI wonder if this is about her sister.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_A_006: Perhaps I said something inappropriate? If so,\nI know what I must do!
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_A_007: Ludia. Is there something about your sister's story of\nlost love that continues to bother you?
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_A_008: *sigh*
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_A_009: If I've somehow upset you, please tell me how\nI can make it up to you.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_A_010: I can tell you still don't get it.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_A_011: But that's fine. It's not something you need to worry\nyourself over. We can't change the past.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_A_012: It's true... I cannot change the past, and I do not\nunderstand much about love.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_A_013: But this much I believe... A heart trapped in the past\nby pain can still find happiness in the future.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_A_014: So please, allow me to assist in this matter.\nI will do everything I can.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_A_015: Ah! Hmm... Was it this plainspoken sincerity you\nfound so endearing, Sister?
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_A_016: And so the last piece of the puzzle falls into place.\nIt seems we sisters have a similar weakness...
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_A_017: The "last piece of the puzzle"? What does that mean?
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_A_018: If you really want to know, follow me.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_A_019: Alright. This is the one. Of all my books, this one\ncontains the most passionate romance of them all.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_A_020: If anything can teach you to recognize love, it'll be\nthis book. Study it to discover the answers you seek.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_A_021: Still compelled to learn about love at my age. But if\nthis is what I must do, then I will do it.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_A_022: Do not worry, Ludia. The Demon Bear shall attack\nthis new challenge without hesitation!
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_A_023: Great! And do try to pay attention to how the other\nwoman feels, alright? I'll be waiting!
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_A_024: Other...woman? I'm not sure what you mean, but\nI'll conquer this task nonetheless.
MID_SE_Lou_Buc_A_025: Now...to begin!